{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CaKCZxeSRNpT34C8SPD4qK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"silicon lattice constant 5.431 Å experimental NIST SRM 640 germanium 5.658 diamond 3.567\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"it.iucr.org\",\"url\":\"https://it.iucr.org/Cb/ch5o2v0001/sec5o2o10/\"},{\"title\":\"xray 2018\",\"url\":\"https://pml.nist.gov/cuu/pdf/xray_2018.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"xray 2018\",\"url\":\"https://www.physics.nist.gov/cuu/pdf/xray_2018.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8596460\"},{\"title\":\"www.cambridge.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/powder-diffraction/article/certification-of-srm-640f-line-position-and-line-shape-standard-for-powder-diffraction/84085B6151B6FB98B485CFBCDEA958B9/share/f0137f2f51535cd695c0c23ef244503685bae50f\"},{\"title\":\"www.cambridge.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/powder-diffraction/article/certification-of-nist-standard-reference-material-640d/BA54AEF9E3CE9DEA0EFA22E5CA3F9763/share/1661e6eccd432300d685528e7865dbd776c0d309\"},{\"title\":\"nist.gov\",\"url\":\"https://tsapps.nist.gov/srmext/certificates/archives/640f.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.cambridge.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/powder-diffraction/article/abs/certification-of-nist-standard-reference-material-640d/BA54AEF9E3CE9DEA0EFA22E5CA3F9763\"},{\"title\":\"cambridgecore.org\",\"url\":\"https://core-prod.cambridgecore.org/core/journals/powder-diffraction/article/certification-of-srm-640f-line-position-and-line-shape-standard-for-powder-diffraction/84085B6151B6FB98B485CFBCDEA958B9\"},{\"title\":\"certification of nist standard reference material 640d\",\"url\":\"https://www-cambridge-org.ezproxyberklee.flo.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/BA54AEF9E3CE9DEA0EFA22E5CA3F9763/S0885715600002256a.pdf/certification-of-nist-standard-reference-material-640d.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search confirms the NIST silicon values but did not return anything on germanium (5.658 Å) or diamond (3.567 Å), so those two numbers remain unverified here.\n\n- **NIST SRM 640c:** A table in the IUCr *International Tables* lists the certified silicon lattice parameter as 5.431195 Å at 295.6 K. It also notes that SRM 640, 640a and 640b are no longer available. The current silicon-powder standard for 2θ calibration is Standard Reference Material (hereinafter abbreviated SRM) 640c.\n- **NIST 2018 adjusted value:** The NIST X-ray wavelength compilation gives an ideal, impurity-free silicon crystal a lattice parameter of 5.431 020 511 Å (in vacuum, 22.5 °C), with a standard uncertainty of 1.6 × 10⁻⁸ relative. This is the value most consistent with your 5.431 Å figure.\n- **SRM 640f:** The current seventh-generation standard has a certified lattice parameter of 0.5431144 nm (5.431144 Å) at 22.5 °C, with an uncertainty of ±0.000008 nm. The source describes it as the seventh generation of this powder diffraction SRM, which is designed to be used primarily for calibrating powder diffractometers with respect to line position.\n- **Sample-to-sample variation:** NIST reports that single-crystal silicon boules are uniform enough for certification, with relative lattice variation indicated by these measurements was ± 4.8 × 10-8 (95 % confidence level).\n\nOverall, the NIST certified silicon values cluster around 5.4311–5.4312 Å, depending on the SRM generation and reference temperature. The 5.431 Å figure is consistent with these. Germanium and diamond values would need a separate search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c1ca279-8286-44c8-8c86-a6e8ad049bf9","uuid":"96b8966f-155f-4a9f-abdf-c1ca482ef724","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:49:59.675Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"silicon lattice constant 5.431 Å experimental NIST SRM 640 germanium 5.658 diamond 3.567","results":[